{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KERFadkpULzaG64Sk59ede","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"worst\" tier scenario. Let me carefully go through the worst tier definition and each planned/remaining experiment.\n\nThe worst tier means:\n1. C1 ablation fails to validate the mask pattern narrative (residual gap too large or BCE 30% ≈ KL)\n2. Core framing doesn't hold, need new angle\n\nKey assumptions for worst:\n- BCE-on-KL-targets at 50% uniform PPL > 15.0, approaching vanilla BCE level — mask quality isn't the main driver\n\n\n- BCE 30% PPL ends up below 10.0 with only a trivial gap from KL 30%, KL 30% uniform shows high variance across seeds (>4 percentage points on MMLU), the 6-point sweep reveals smooth degradation without any sharp phase transition, and multiple reviewers flag that the method is incremental with no wall-clock speedup gains and an unexplained 14B model gap\n- Some of the sparsity variants and BCE training runs either fail or remain incomplete\n\nNow I'm going through the planned and remaining experiments from the experiment_plan to map out what predicted data each one should generate under this worst-case scenario. Looking at the planned experiments in the plan, I need to expand detailed data for plan_010 (LongBench), plan_011 (MT-Bench), and plan_012 (RULER). I'm also tracking the what_if experiments like the ablation studies and sparsity sweeps, plus the PREPARING items in the registry that are still in progress.\n\nNow I'm working through worst-case predictions for each experiment. For the C1 ablation with uniform 50% allocation, the baseline shows 9.29 PPL at the model's native 61% sparsity, but forcing it to 50% uniform would degrade performance significantly since the learned sparsity patterns wouldn't align with the uniform constraint—I'd expect PPL to exceed 15.0, approaching vanilla BCE performance.\n\nThe key insight here is that mask quality alone isn't what drives KL's advantage; rather, it's the optimization dynamics during KL training that matter. Even when BCE gets the \"right\" target masks from KL, it still underperforms at 50% uniform, suggesting the gradient flow and learning process itself is what makes KL superior.\n\nNow I'm considering the alternative worst-case scenario: if BCE at 30% sparsity performs nearly as well as KL, then KL wouldn't have any meaningful advantage at the recommended operating point. Looking at the ablation data, BCE on KL targets achieves 9.29 PPL at 60.9% sparsity with strong oracle agreement, which is already quite competitive compared to KL's performance at 50%.\n\nThe puzzle is how this could degrade to PPL > 15.0 at uniform 50% sparsity when it's already at 9.29 with per-token sparsity—the distribution mismatch between the predictor's native behavior and forced uniform sparsity might explain the gap, though a jump that large seems extreme. The key insight is that the BCE predictor was trained on KL-derived oracle masks with 97.8% agreement, so it learned to closely mimic the KL oracle's behavior. Well, the 9.29 result was at the native ~61% sparsity the predictor chose, so moving to 50% uniform changes both the sparsity level and allocation strategy. Lower sparsity should improve PPL, but uniform allocation might hurt performance compared to the global top-k approach the model was trained on, creating tension between these two effects.\n\nLooking at the C1 ablation more carefully, BCE at 30% is nearly equivalent to KL at 30%, which would make KL's advantage negligible at the recommended operating point. At 50% uniform, the mask pattern does seem to help — PPL around 12-13 beats vanilla BCE's 22-28 range but still falls short of KL's 11.8. The residual gap is substantial enough that it's unclear whether mask quality alone explains the difference, or if the remaining advantage comes from the optimization process itself or just experimental noise. The high variance in downstream metrics and smooth degradation across sparsity levels undermine any robustness claims, while the mask pattern narrative collapses since BCE can't match KL's performance even with KL-derived targets, and the practical gap shrinks to marginal at the recommended 30% operating point. Now I'm mapping out all the pending experiments to establish what predictions I need to make for each one. Looking at the experiment_plan entries, plans 010 through 012 are marked as planned, and I can see several related experiments in the registry that are currently preparing—the sparsity sweeps, the ablation evaluation, and the BCE forced topk variant. These appear to be the remaining work that needs detailed predictions.\n\nFor the c1_ablation_eval_uniform case, I'm expecting worse performance because forcing a uniform 50% sparsity pattern breaks the learned mask structure that KL optimization discovered. Even though the oracle agreement was strong at native sparsity, the uniform constraint exposes how much the model relied on that specific pattern—BCE can't recover the same optimization trajectory that KL found through its coupled gradient flow, so I'd predict PPL around 15.8, well above the 15.0 threshold.\n\nAt 30% sparsity with BCE, the task becomes much easier since most neurons survive anyway, so the per-neuron independence of BCE matters less. The performance gap versus KL shrinks to roughly 1.0 PPL point, which actually weakens the argument that KL provides unique value at this operating point—I'd expect PPL around 9.8.\n\nFor the 25% sparsity KL experiment, training appears unstable or partially fails, yielding PPL around 7.6 with MMLU performance at 42%.\n\nThe Lagrangian controller struggles to hit the exact 25% target, likely settling around 22-24% actual sparsity instead, which creates a messy data point that doesn't align cleanly with the sweep. The 35% and 45% sparsity points show smooth interpolation between their neighbors with no surprising behavior—PPL values of 8.5 and 10.1 respectively, falling right where I'd expect them in the curve.\n\nWhen I aggregate all six points together, the data reveals something important: what looked like a phase transition at 40% was actually just an artifact of sparse sampling. With the intermediate points filled in, the relationship becomes clearly continuous and approximately quadratic, fitting a simple curve with R²=0.95. The piecewise three-regime model only marginally improves this to R²=0.65 for the segment-identification test, which doesn't justify the added complexity. The smooth degradation across the full range suggests there's no meaningful structural break in how the model behaves as sparsity increases.\n\nThe 50% sparsity point with different seeds confirms the pattern holds—PPL around 11.85 is consistent across runs, and downstream performance matches what I see elsewhere.\n\nNow looking at long-context performance with LongBench, the picture gets much worse. The KL sparse approach degrades significantly across all task types compared to dense baselines, with drops of 40-50% depending on the task. Dense models achieve narrativeqa around 7.3, qasper around 13.4, and gov_report around 30.5, but KL sparse at 30% uniform drops those to roughly 4.1, 6.2, and 17.0 respectively. This makes sense because the predictor was trained on 2048-token sequences, so tasks ranging from 4K to 32K tokens are fundamentally out-of-distribution. The non-uniform quality drops across different task types make it hard to claim the approach is ready for deployment in long-context scenarios.\n\nMT-Bench shows a similar story—KL sparse scores around 4.5-5.0 versus dense performance around 6.\n\n5-7.0. Multi-turn instruction following compounds the noise problem since sparse inference introduces per-token errors that accumulate across conversation turns, creating a gap large enough that reviewers would flag it as a practical limitation.\n\nRULER follows the same pattern with sharp degradation beyond 4K tokens, again pointing back to the fundamental issue that a predictor trained on short sequences doesn't generalize well to longer contexts.\n\nFor the MMLU analysis with KL 30% uniform across three seeds, I'm rechecking the numbers—seed 42 gives 40.61, seed 123 gives 37.63, and seed 456 gives 37.27.\n\nComputing the mean and standard deviation across these three runs, I get a mean of 38.50 with a standard deviation of 1.83 percentage points. That's actually below the 4pp threshold I'd expect for the worst tier, which creates a discrepancy since the worst tier prediction should show σ > 4pp.\n\nWait, I'm realizing these are already measured values from completed experiments, but the user is asking me to predict outcomes for planned experiments under worst-case assumptions. The existing data gives me a baseline for what's realistic, but for the experiments that haven't been run yet, I need to project what worst-case performance would look like. Let me reconsider what the user is actually asking for—they want predictions across all experiments in the plan, not just the ones already completed.\n\nSo I need to identify which experiments are still in the planning or preparation phase and then construct worst-case projections for each of them based on the worst tier definition.\n\nLooking at the remaining work, I've got five KL sparsity experiments at different levels, plus the KL50 variant, three benchmark evaluations (LongBench, MT-Bench, RULER), and a few analysis-based experiments that reuse data from the main runs. Now I'm thinking through what the worst-case scenario would look like for each of these — essentially, what if performance degraded more than expected across all the metrics that matter.\n\nI also need to figure out which tables and figures to include in the final output, which depends on what the paper is actually focusing on. be redundant since both the training and evaluation components are already finished. Now I'm mapping out the remaining experiments that actually need to run and constructing worst-case scenarios for each one. The key failure modes I'm tracking are whether the C1 ablation breaks the mask pattern explanation, whether BCE at 30% matches KL's performance too closely, high variance in MMLU results, and whether we see any sharp transitions or just smooth degradation. I'm also considering what happens if some runs don't complete and how reviewers might perceive the overall contribution given the incremental nature and lack of wall-clock improvements.\n\nFor the worst-case tier, I need both conditions to fail simultaneously: the C1 ablation showing that mask patterns don't transfer well across objectives, and the BCE 30% result being trivially close to KL's performance. Setting C1 uniform PPL at 16.2 and BCE 30% at 9.6 creates maximum damage because it undermines both the mask quality narrative and the advantage at the recommended operating point.\n\nNow I'm looking at the intermediate sparsity levels—25%, 35%, and 45%—to see if they show a smooth degradation pattern or support the three-regime story. The existing data points at 30%, 40%, and 50% give me anchors, and I need to fill in the gaps to determine whether the transition is gradual or sharp.\n\nBut there's a complication: some of these experiments might have actually failed during training, particularly at the lower sparsity targets where the Lagrangian optimization struggles to converge. So the \"worst\" scenario isn't just about poor performance—it's also about incomplete results that would leave gaps in the narrative.\n\nLet me map out what I expect for the worst tier: the uniform ablation will show PPL degradation that breaks the sparsity-performance story, the BCE variant will be too similar to KL to be interesting, and the lower sparsity targets might fail outright or produce unstable results that can't be reliably reported.\n\nFor the downstream evaluations, I'm seeing a clear pattern where aggressive sparsity hits quality hard—LongBench drops 40-55%, MT-Bench scores crater from 6.8 to 4.8, and RULER shows sharp cliffs past 4K tokens. The aggregate sweep analysis suggests smooth degradation without any sudden phase transitions, which is actually useful for the narrative even if the absolute numbers aren't great.\n\nI should skip the KL 50% eval since those metrics are already in the system, then focus on pulling downstream numbers for the sparsity sweep points to complete the picture.\n\nNow I'm accounting for the multi-reviewer feedback about incremental methods lacking wall-clock speedup and the unexplained 14B gap—that's going to pull the expected ARR down to 2.5-3.0 range, which I need to reflect in the worst-case scenario. For that tier, the narrative should pivot toward one of the backup directions rather than doubling down on the current approach.\n\nLooking at what the user actually asked for, I need to cover every planned experiment in the experiment_plan: that's plan_010, plan_011, plan_012 from the main pipeline, plus the what_if experiments and the PREPARING registry items that feed into them. I'm organizing the imagined_experiments to trace those dependencies—like c1_ablation_eval_uniform feeding into the BCE-KL what_if, and bce_30pct_s42_eval supporting the forced topk variant.\n\nWriting the full output now...\n\nGenerating YAML structure... Looking at the actual measured MMLU data across seeds, the uniform allocation shows much lower variance at 1.83pp than the worst-case threshold of 4pp, but when I examine the global allocation strategy instead, the results are far more scattered across the three seeds, which better explains the robustness concerns flagged in the worst-case scenario. The global allocation approach shows massive variance (σ = 9.57pp) with one seed performing much worse than others, which actually supports the worst-case narrative that the method is fragile without uniform allocation. I'm getting pulled into the weeds here though—I should just focus on writing out the YAML predictions now. Let me look back at the completed kl_sparsity30 experiments to make sure my predictions for the 25/35/45 variants are internally consistent with what actually happened.\n\nLooking at the results, kl_sparsity30 struggled to hit its target—the Lagrangian capped out at lambda=1000 in one run but succeeded at lambda=5000 in another with PPL around 7.3. The initial sparsity before training sits around 40%, so targeting 25% means pushing sparsity down significantly, while 50% means pushing it up slightly. Counterintuitively, lower sparsity targets should be easier since they require less aggressive pruning, yet the 30% target still caused issues—the real problem seems to be something else about how the Lagrangian handles these constraints.\n\nI suspect the issue is that lambda gets driven too high, overwhelming the loss function and destabilizing training. For the worst-case tier, I'm predicting kl_sparsity25 will fail entirely with lambda saturation and oscillating sparsity, while kl_sparsity35 should succeed around 0.33 sparsity with PPL ~9.3, and kl_sparsity45 should hit ~0.43 sparsity with PPL ~10.4. The BCE 30% run is already complete.\n\nWith the eval showing PPL around 9.6, I'll have four solid data points (30/35/40/45) plus the existing 50, which means the 25 point is missing. That's still enough to see the smooth curve and phase transition pattern, even without the full six points.\n\nNow I'm ready to write this up. For the LongBench experiments, there have been six failed attempts and one partial success—the dense v6 baseline shows narrativeqa at 7.3, qasper at 13.4, gov_report at 30.5, and multi_news at 2.5, while the KL-regularized version performed much worse with narrativeqa dropping to 4.12, qasper to 6.23, gov_report to 16.97, and multi_news to 18.01, indicating the KL constraint is significantly hurting performance on this benchmark.\n\nLooking at the worst-case projections across the remaining benchmarks, I'm seeing consistent 40-55% degradation with multi-document QA and code tasks hit especially hard, plus qualitative failures in long-dependency reasoning. For MT-Bench under worst conditions, the dense baseline would be around 6.8, KL 30% uniform drops to 4.5, and KL 50% global falls to 3.2, with the multi-turn format amplifying per-token errors. On RULER, degradation accelerates beyond 4K tokens, hitting near-random accuracy on multi-hop tasks at 16K, suggesting the predictor breaks down on longer sequences.\n\nNow I need to structure this into the final YAML output, though I'm reconsidering how to organize it best. The mask pattern narrative falls apart with both the C1 ablation results and the forced topk experiments, so I need to abandon that angle and pivot toward either a practical deployment guide or an optimization landscape analysis instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34575,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34575},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9d7294e-da79-48fd-83a0-93196cf1e3dc","uuid":"9ba999d6-eba8-43d7-af45-0dc8e37c9662"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KERFadkpULzaG64Sk59ede","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  'Mask pattern discovery' framing 全面失败。C1 ablation 两条腿同时断裂：50% uniform 下\n  BCE-on-KL-targets PPL ≈ 16+（mask 质量不足以解释 KL 优势），30% forced top-k 下 BCE PPL ≈ 9.6\n  （与 KL 8.82 差距 trivial，KL 在推荐操作点无独特价值）。6-point sweep 无 phase transition，\n  三 regime 叙事退化为 smooth quadratic。此时必须 pivot。推荐方向 (A) practical deployment guide：\n  paper 核心变为 3-model × 4-sparsity × 2-allocation × 2-loss controlled study，贡献是 actionable recipe，\n  title 类似 \"When Does KL Distillation Help Sparse Inference? A Controlled Study\"。\n  所有已有实验数据（含 negative results）重新组织为 recipe 维度。3-5 天重写 §1-§3，无需新实验。\n  ARR 2.5-3.0，冲 Findings 或 Industry Track 更稳。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: c1_ablation_eval_uniform\n    plan_id: c1_ablation_bce_kl_targets\n    description: >\n      C1 ablation 核心实验：用 KL-derived oracle masks 训练的 BCE predictor，在 50% uniform allocation\n      下评估。测试 mask pattern quality 是否足以解释 KL 优势。\n    expected_results:\n      wt2_ppl_uniform_50pct: 16.2\n      wt2_ppl_global_50pct: 15.4\n      reference_kl_50pct_uniform_ppl: 11.96\n      reference_vanilla_bce_50pct_ppl: 22.51\n      residual_gap_vs_kl: 4.24\n      residual_gap_vs_vanilla_bce: 6.31\n      mask_quality_explains_pct: 59.4\n      optimization_process_explains_pct: 40.6\n      oracle_agreement_at_50pct_uniform: 0.91\n      eval_sparsity: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      c1_ablation_bce_kl_targets_s42 在 native ~61% sparsity 下 PPL=9.29、oracle agreement=97.8%，\n      看似 mask transfer 成功。但该结果是 per-token sparsity 下的 best-case——predictor 自行选择\n      pruning 分布。强制 50% uniform allocation 改变了两个维度：(1) sparsity level 从 61% 降到 50%\n      理应降低 PPL，但 (2) uniform allocation 移除了 predictor 的 per-layer adaptive budget，\n      暴露 BCE 优化器在 off-distribution allocation 下的脆弱性。\n      关键机制：KL 训练时全 forward pass 的 coupled gradient 让 predictor 隐式学会了 allocation-robust\n      的 mask pattern，而 BCE 仅学到 per-neuron 的 binary classification boundary——在 native sparsity\n      下精确匹配 oracle，但换 allocation 策略后迅速退化。oracle agreement 从 97.8% 降至 ~91%，\n      看似只有 7pp 差异，但在 50% sparsity 的 critical regime 下这 7% 的 mask error 被放大。\n      PPL 16.2 高于 KL 的 11.96（gap=4.24），但显著低于 vanilla BCE 的 22.51（gap=6.31），\n      说明 mask quality 解释了约 59% 的 KL 优势，剩余 41% 归因于 optimization process。\n      这个 59/41 的分割恰恰是 worst case——既不能说 \"mask pattern is everything\"（residual gap 4.24 太大），\n      也不能说 \"mask pattern is nothing\"（确实帮了 6.31 PPL），无法支撑任何简洁叙事。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 3 (C1 Ablation): 新增行 'BCE-on-KL-targets, 50% uniform' PPL=16.2，与 KL uniform=11.96、vanilla BCE=22.51 对比\"\n      - \"Table 1 (Main Results): 无法新增，但 C1 ablation 的 ambiguous 结果削弱 Table 1 中 KL vs BCE 的 framing\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4 bar chart: 三条柱 KL(11.96) / BCE-on-KL-targets(16.2) / vanilla-BCE(22.51)，中间柱的高度让 'mask quality explains KL advantage' 叙事无法成立\"\n    analysis: >\n      mask quality 解释了 KL 优势的 ~60%，但剩余 ~40% 的 gap 过大。Reviewer 会问：'so what IS the\n      explanation?'——而我们既不能说 gradient coupling（§3.6 已降为 suggestive），也不能说 mask pattern\n      （C1 ablation 刚打脸）。framing 陷入 no-man's-land。\n\n  - name: bce_30pct_forced_topk\n    plan_id: bce_30pct_forced_topk\n    description: >\n      BCE predictor 在 30% sparsity 下通过 TEAL forced top-k 评估。填 Table 2 gap，\n      测试 KL 在推荐操作点是否有独特价值。\n    expected_results:\n      wt2_ppl_teal_global_30pct: 9.62\n      reference_kl_30pct_uniform_ppl: 8.82\n      reference_teal_vanilla_30pct_ppl: 10.97\n      ppl_gap_vs_kl: 0.80\n      ppl_gap_vs_teal_vanilla: 1.35\n      arc_challenge_acc_norm: 0.398\n      winogrande_acc: 0.661\n      mmlu_acc: 0.362\n      gsm8k_exact_match: 0.071\n      actual_sparsity: 0.30\n    result_rationale: >\n      30% sparsity 是 budget-surplus regime——保留 70% 神经元，任务本质上 \"太容易\"。\n      BCE 在 50% 下训练时（bce_isocompute_v3 系列）PPL=27-28，灾难性；但 30% forced top-k\n      完全不同：(1) TEAL allocation 在 30% 下更均匀（每层保留 ≥60%），per-neuron BCE scoring\n      与 global top-k 的冲突小得多；(2) magnitude-based scoring 在低 sparsity 下本身就够好\n      （TEAL vanilla 30%=10.97 vs 50%=23.31，差 2×），BCE 的 learned scoring 只需微小改进\n      就能接近 KL；(3) 现有 kl_bce_f1_oracle 数据显示 BCE F1=0.61 vs KL=0.54——BCE 在\n      per-neuron 精度上实际更高，只是在 global reallocation 下这种精度优势被削弱。\n      在 30% 这种\"奢侈\"sparsity 下，per-neuron 精度 ≈ global quality，所以 BCE 和 KL 收敛。\n      PPL gap 仅 0.80（KL 8.82 vs BCE 9.62），MMLU gap ~4pp（KL 40.6% vs BCE 36.2%），\n      均在 noise margin 内。Reviewer 会直接问：\"why not just use BCE at 30%?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (Sparsity Sweep): 新增 BCE 30% 行，PPL=9.62，与 KL 30%=8.82 并列\"\n      - \"Table 5 (Downstream): BCE 30% downstream 与 KL 30% 差距全部 <5pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: BCE 30% 点紧贴 KL 30% 点，两者在 PPL-efficiency 曲线上几乎重叠，KL 的 Pareto 优势仅在 ≥40% 才显现\"\n    analysis: >\n      KL 在推荐操作点（30%）的独特价值蒸发。PPL 差 0.80、MMLU 差 ~4pp——一个 reviewer 可以\n      argue this is meaningful，但另一个会说 \"within noise / trivial\"。关键问题：如果 30% 是\n      practical recommendation，而 KL 和 BCE 在 30% 表现相当，那 paper 的 contribution 是什么？\n      只有 ≥50% 才能看到 KL 的大幅优势，但 50% 的 downstream collapse 使该操作点无部署价值。\n\n  - name: kl_sparsity25_s42\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      KL predictor 训练 target=25% sparsity。6-point sweep 的最低 sparsity 点。\n    expected_results:\n      status: failed\n      actual_sparsity: 0.208\n      target_sparsity: 0.25\n      lambda_final: 5000\n      lambda_max_cap: 5000\n      constraint_satisfied: false\n      sparsity_trajectory: \"40%→28%→22%→21%→20.8%, stuck\"\n      wt2_ppl: null\n      training_steps: 1000\n      wall_clock_sec: 2700\n      failure_mode: \"Lagrangian cannot push sparsity to 25% — predictor architecture has implicit floor ~20% from natural activation patterns\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      kl_sparsity30 的历史已经预示了这个失败：v1 和 v2 都卡在 28.1%（target 30%），v3 靠\n      lambda_max=5000 才勉强到 28.5%。25% target 更难——需要保留 75% 的神经元，而 predictor\n      的 initial state（从 random init 经 Gumbel-sigmoid）天然倾向 ~40% sparsity。\n      Lagrangian 需要把 sparsity 从 40% 压到 25%，意味着 lambda 必须主导 loss landscape，\n      压制 KL divergence objective。但当 lambda 过大时，predictor 退化为 \"全开\" 模式，\n      sparsity 从 40% 降到 ~21% 后触底——这是 SwiGLU gate activation 的 natural floor，\n      即使不做任何 pruning 也有 ~20% 的神经元 gate value ≈ 0。\n      结果：无法评估、Table 有空缺。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 25% 行标注 '†训练未收敛' 或留空\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sweep curve 缺少最左端数据点，5 点而非 6 点\"\n    analysis: >\n      关键空缺。没有 25% 数据点意味着：(1) 无法确认 sweep 曲线左端行为；(2) Reviewer 会质疑\n      method 在低 sparsity 下的 applicability；(3) 5 点 vs 6 点对 piecewise fit 的 statistical\n      power 进一步下降。\n\n  - name: kl_sparsity35_s42\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      KL predictor 训练 target=35% sparsity。填补 30%-40% 之间的中间点。\n    expected_results:\n      actual_sparsity: 0.337\n      target_sparsity: 0.35\n      lambda_final: 3000\n      constraint_satisfied: true\n      wt2_ppl_pertoken: 8.05\n      wt2_ppl_teal_global: 9.42\n      wt2_ppl_uniform: 8.28\n      arc_challenge_acc_norm: 0.412\n      winogrande_acc: 0.672\n      mmlu_acc: 0.351\n      gsm8k_exact_match: 0.058\n      training_steps: 1000\n    result_rationale: >\n      35% 在 30% 和 40% 之间，Lagrangian 应能收敛（30% 最终成功，40% 直接成功）。\n      PPL 预测基于已有数据的 smooth interpolation：30% global=8.98、40% global=10.12，\n      线性插值给出 ~9.5，但实际曲线在低 sparsity 端略 concave（KL 在 budget-surplus 下\n      性能降解更缓慢），所以 35% global ≈ 9.42。这恰恰是 worst case 的关键证据——\n      35% 点完美落在 30% 和 40% 的线性插值上，没有任何 inflection point 或 regime boundary。\n      如果存在 phase transition，应该在 30%-40% 之间看到斜率突变，但 35% 的 PPL 9.42\n      精确匹配线性趋势。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 35% 行 PPL=9.42\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sweep curve: 35% 点落在 30%-40% 的线性连接线上，无 inflection\"\n    analysis: >\n      最具破坏力的数据点。35% 的 smooth interpolation 直接否定了 \"budget-surplus → budget-constrained\n      regime boundary exists between 30-40%\" 的说法。原叙事中 30% uniform wins、40% global wins\n      的 \"non-monotonic allocation preference\" 现在看起来只是 noise——35% 的 allocation preference\n      如果也是 ambiguous（uniform 和 global 差距 <2pp），那 regime boundary 就不存在。\n\n  - name: kl_sparsity45_s42\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      KL predictor 训练 target=45% sparsity。填补 40%-50% 之间的中间点。\n    expected_results:\n      actual_sparsity: 0.432\n      target_sparsity: 0.45\n      lambda_final: 5000\n      constraint_satisfied: false\n      wt2_ppl_pertoken: 9.81\n      wt2_ppl_teal_global: 10.65\n      wt2_ppl_uniform: 10.32\n      arc_challenge_acc_norm: 0.368\n      winogrande_acc: 0.648\n      mmlu_acc: 0.298\n      gsm8k_exact_match: 0.032\n      training_steps: 1000\n      sparsity_note: \"actual 43.2% vs target 45%, Lagrangian undershoots by 1.8pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      45% 介于 40%（成功，actual=39.8%）和 50%（成功，actual=49.8%）之间。Lagrangian\n      略有 undershoot（1.8pp），类似 30% 的情况但不严重到 fail。PPL 10.65 global\n      在 40% 的 10.12 和 50% 的 11.79 之间 smooth interpolation。\n      关键在下游：MMLU 29.8% 已经接近 random（25%），但 40% 时还有 38.1%。如果存在\n      \"capacity cliff\" phase transition，应该在 45% 看到 MMLU 从 38% 急跌到 ~28%，\n      但实际上 45% 给出 29.8%——这是 smooth degradation 而非 cliff。40%→45% MMLU\n      差 8.3pp、45%→50% 差 2.1pp，斜率 decreasing 而非 increasing，说明是 approaching\n      asymptote（random baseline）而非 phase transition。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 45% 行 PPL=10.65, MMLU=29.8%\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sweep curve: 45% 点继续 smooth 趋势，MMLU 曲线 approaching random floor without sharp transition\"\n    analysis: >\n      MMLU 的 \"cliff\" 在数据 densification 后消失。40%→50% 看似 dramatic drop（38.1→27.8，\n      -10.3pp），但加入 45%（29.8%）后变成两段 smooth decline：40→45 降 8.3pp、45→50 降 2.0pp。\n      不是 cliff，是 gradual approach to random floor。\n\n  - name: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt_aggregate\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      6-point sweep 聚合分析：25%/30%/35%/40%/45%/50%。Piecewise regression 测试\n      三 regime 叙事 vs smooth quadratic。\n    expected_results:\n      available_points: 5\n      missing_points: [\"25%\"]\n      ppl_values_global:\n        sp30: 8.98\n        sp35: 9.42\n        sp40: 10.12\n        sp45: 10.65\n        sp50: 11.79\n      quadratic_fit_r2: 0.987\n      piecewise_3segment_fit_r2: 0.993\n      piecewise_improvement_over_quadratic: 0.006\n      f_test_pvalue_piecewise_vs_quadratic: 0.42\n      regime_boundary_30_40_evidence: \"none — 35% interpolates linearly\"\n      regime_boundary_40_50_evidence: \"none — 45% interpolates linearly\"\n      mmlu_values:\n        sp30_uniform: 0.406\n        sp35: 0.351\n        sp40_global: 0.381\n        sp45: 0.298\n        sp50_uniform: 0.278\n      mmlu_smooth_degradation: true\n      mmlu_phase_transition_evidence: \"none — monotonic decline approaching random floor\"\n      allocation_preference_at_35pct: \"ambiguous (uniform 8.28 vs global 9.42, confounded by sparsity mismatch)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      5 个可用数据点（25% 缺失）的 PPL sweep 完美拟合 quadratic：PPL ≈ 6.12 + 0.03s + 0.15s²\n      （s = sparsity %），R² = 0.987。Piecewise 3-segment 拟合 R² = 0.993，比 quadratic\n      仅提升 0.006，F-test p=0.42 远不显著——增加两个 breakpoint 参数不 justified。\n      原叙事的三 regime 基于 3 个点（30/40/50）的 apparent inflection，但 densified sampling\n      填入 35% 和 45% 后，所有 \"inflection\" 消失为 smooth curve。MMLU 的下降也是 monotonic：\n      40.6→35.1→38.1→29.8→27.8，40% 的 38.1% 看似 \"recovery\"，但那是 global allocation\n      的效果（之前 30% 用 uniform），allocation × sparsity confound 未被控制。\n      在所有 sparsity 用同一 allocation 评估后（e.g., 全用 global），MMLU 严格递减，无 non-monotonicity。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 完整 5-point sweep，右侧列标注 quadratic fit residuals\"\n      - \"Table S1 (Supplementary): Piecewise vs quadratic fit comparison statistics\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: PPL vs sparsity scatter + quadratic fit curve (R²=0.987)，无 visible phase transition\"\n      - \"Fig 5b: MMLU vs sparsity，monotonic decline approaching 25% floor，与 PPL 趋势一致\"\n      - \"Fig S1: Residual plot of piecewise vs quadratic，residuals indistinguishable\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 regime 叙事不成立。数据支持的 simplest model 是 smooth quadratic degradation。\n      \"Non-monotonic allocation preference\" 是 allocation × sparsity confound 的 artifact——\n      在控制 allocation 后消失。Reviewer 2 会写：\"The claimed phase transition is not\n      supported by the data. A simple quadratic fits equally well.\"\n\n  - name: plan_010_longbench\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      LongBench English subset (4K-32K tokens)。所有条件（KL-only, BCE+comp, SPON, SPON+KL,\n      training-free baselines）。测试 predictor 在长序列上的泛化能力。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_narrativeqa: 7.3\n      dense_qasper: 13.4\n      dense_gov_report: 30.5\n      dense_multi_news: 2.5\n      dense_avg: 13.4\n      kl_30_uniform_narrativeqa: 4.1\n      kl_30_uniform_qasper: 6.2\n      kl_30_uniform_gov_report: 17.0\n      kl_30_uniform_multi_news: 18.0\n      kl_30_uniform_avg: 11.3\n      kl_50_global_narrativeqa: 1.8\n      kl_50_global_qasper: 2.1\n      kl_50_global_gov_report: 8.4\n      kl_50_global_multi_news: 14.2\n      kl_50_global_avg: 6.6\n      teal_30_narrativeqa: 3.5\n      teal_30_qasper: 5.8\n      teal_30_gov_report: 15.2\n      teal_30_multi_news: 16.8\n      teal_30_avg: 10.3\n      teal_50_narrativeqa: 0.9\n      teal_50_qasper: 1.2\n      teal_50_gov_report: 4.1\n      teal_50_multi_news: 10.5\n      teal_50_avg: 4.2\n      kl_30_vs_dense_retention: 0.55\n      kl_50_vs_dense_retention: 0.31\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_advantage: \"+1.0 avg (+9.7%)\"\n      multi_news_anomaly: \"KL 30% multi_news=18.0 > dense=2.5，疑似 format mismatch / generation collapse into repetitive text inflating ROUGE\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      longbench_dense_v6 和 longbench_kl30_uniform_v6 的已有数据已经暗示了问题：\n      (1) dense baseline 本身就很弱（narrativeqa=7.3，相比 GPT-4 的 ~25），说明 Llama-3.1-8B\n      在 LongBench 上不是 competitive baseline；(2) KL 30% 相对 dense 下降 ~45%（avg 11.3 vs 13.4），\n      虽然比 TEAL 好一点，但绝对值太低没有实用意义。\n      更糟糕的是 multi_news 异常：KL 30% 得分 18.0 远高于 dense 的 2.5。这几乎必然是评估 bug\n      ——sparse model 生成退化为重复文本，而 ROUGE-L 对重复文本敏感（与 reference 中重复出现的\n      n-gram 匹配），导致假高分。这个 anomaly 会被 reviewer 抓住，要求重新评估。\n      整体来看：KL vs TEAL 的 advantage 在长序列上仅 ~10%（远低于 short-context 的 ~25%），\n      且所有 sparse 方法在 LongBench 上表现都很差——这是 sparse inference 的 fundamental limitation，\n      不是我们的 method 特有问题，但 reviewer 不关心这个区分。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 6 (LongBench): 4 tasks × 5 conditions，dense 作为上界，大面积红色（显著退化）\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: LongBench per-task grouped bar chart，所有 sparse 方法的 bars 都远低于 dense\"\n      - \"Fig 7 inset: KL 30% vs TEAL 30% 的 relative advantage（+10%）在长序列上收窄到在 short-context 的一半以下\"\n    analysis: >\n      LongBench 结果对论文的两个打击：(1) 绝对性能太低，reviewer 会质疑 \"这种 quality 水平\n      有什么部署价值\"；(2) KL 的相对优势在长序列上缩小，因为 predictor 是在 2048-token\n      序列上训练的，超出训练长度后 prediction quality 下降。这暴露了一个未在论文中讨论的\n      limitation：sparse predictor 的 sequence-length generalization。\n\n  - name: plan_011_mtbench\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      MT-Bench 评估 (GPT-4o judge)。80 multi-turn questions, 8 categories。\n      测试 instruction-following quality under sparsity。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_score: 6.82\n      kl_30_uniform_score: 5.41\n      kl_50_global_score: 3.68\n      teal_30_score: 5.12\n      teal_50_score: 2.95\n      bce_isocompute_50_score: 3.22\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_delta: \"+0.29\"\n      category_breakdown_kl_30:\n        writing: 6.1\n        roleplay: 5.8\n        reasoning: 4.2\n        math: 3.1\n        coding: 4.5\n        extraction: 6.3\n        stem: 5.2\n        humanities: 5.9\n      turn2_degradation_kl_30: \"-0.8 vs turn1\"\n      turn2_degradation_kl_50: \"-1.9 vs turn1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      MT-Bench 测试 multi-turn coherence，sparse inference 的 per-token noise 在多轮中累积。\n      dense Llama-3.1-8B MT-Bench 典型分 ~6.8。KL 30% 在 short-context PPL 上只差 0.82\n      （8.82 vs 6.12，ratio 1.44），但 MT-Bench 是生成任务——PPL 的 1.44 ratio 在 autoregressive\n      decoding 中累积，每个 token 的 slightly-wrong prediction 会 compound。\n      30% sparsity 下 turn-1 约 5.8，turn-2 降到 ~5.0（turn-2 依赖 turn-1 的 generated context，\n      sparse prediction 引入的 drift 在 turn-2 放大）。平均 5.41。\n      关键：KL 30% vs TEAL 30% 只差 0.29（5.41 vs 5.12）——在 MT-Bench 的 1-10 scale 上\n      这是 noise-level 差异，GPT-4o judge 的 inter-rater reliability 约 ±0.5。\n      Reviewer 可以 legitimately claim \"KL and TEAL are indistinguishable on generation quality\n      at 30% sparsity\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 7 (MT-Bench): 5 conditions × overall + 8 categories\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: MT-Bench radar chart，dense(外圈) vs KL-30%(中圈) vs TEAL-30%(内圈)，math/reasoning 象限 collapse 明显\"\n      - \"Fig 8b: Turn-1 vs Turn-2 degradation，sparse 方法的 turn-2 drop 显著大于 dense\"\n    analysis: >\n      MT-Bench 进一步弱化 KL 的 practical value proposition：在 generation quality（用户真正\n      感知的维度）上，KL 30% 和 TEAL 30% 的差距远小于 PPL 暗示的差距。这支持了 \"PPL is a\n      poor proxy for downstream generation quality\" 的说法——但该说法反过来也削弱了论文自身\n      以 PPL 为核心指标的可信度。math/reasoning 的 severe degradation 是 expected（这些任务\n      对 per-token accuracy 最敏感），但 reviewer 会关注这些 high-visibility categories。\n\n  - name: plan_012_ruler\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      RULER synthetic long-context (4K, 16K) × 3 task types。\n      Fine-grained capability diagnostics complementing LongBench。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_4k_niah: 0.95\n      dense_4k_vt: 0.82\n      dense_4k_cwe: 0.78\n      dense_16k_niah: 0.88\n      dense_16k_vt: 0.61\n      dense_16k_cwe: 0.52\n      kl_30_4k_niah: 0.89\n      kl_30_4k_vt: 0.71\n      kl_30_4k_cwe: 0.65\n      kl_30_16k_niah: 0.62\n      kl_30_16k_vt: 0.38\n      kl_30_16k_cwe: 0.29\n      kl_50_4k_niah: 0.72\n      kl_50_4k_vt: 0.48\n      kl_50_4k_cwe: 0.41\n      kl_50_16k_niah: 0.35\n      kl_50_16k_vt: 0.21\n      kl_50_16k_cwe: 0.15\n      teal_30_4k_niah: 0.86\n      teal_30_4k_vt: 0.67\n      teal_30_4k_cwe: 0.59\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_avg_4k: \"+4.3pp\"\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_avg_16k: \"+2.1pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RULER 的 NIAH (needle-in-a-haystack) 是 attention-dependent task，sparsity 主要影响\n      FFN 而非 attention，所以 4K 下退化相对温和（KL 30%: 0.89 vs dense 0.95）。\n      但 VT (variable tracking) 和 CWE (common-words extraction) 需要 cross-position reasoning，\n      FFN 的 capacity loss 通过 attention→FFN→attention 链式传播。16K 下所有 tasks 严重退化：\n      KL 30% NIAH 0.62（vs dense 0.88，-26pp），说明 predictor 在长序列中段的 attention output\n      分布 shift 超出训练时见过的范围。\n      KL vs TEAL 的 advantage 在 4K 下 ~4pp，16K 下缩小到 ~2pp——与 LongBench 一致：\n      predictor 的泛化优势随序列长度衰减。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 8 (RULER): 3 tasks × 2 lengths × 4 conditions\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: RULER heatmap (task × length × condition)，颜色从绿(dense)到红(sparse 50%)，16K 列大面积红色\"\n    analysis: >\n      RULER 诊断出精确的失败模式：不是 \"sparse model cannot do long-context\"（4K 下还行），\n      而是 \"predictor trained on 2K cannot generalize to 16K\"。这是一个 fixable limitation\n      （train on longer sequences），但在当前论文中是 open gap。reviewer 12 会建议 future work。\n      更根本的问题：RULER 让 \"sparse inference as deployment-ready\" 的 narrative 难以为继——\n      实际部署需要 long-context capability，而我们的 method 在 16K 下退化 ~30-40%。\n\n  - name: kl_30pct_3seed_robustness\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      KL 30% uniform 3-seed robustness 分析（已有数据汇总 + 新 seed 预测）。\n      测试 headline numbers 的可复现性。\n    expected_results:\n      seed_42_mmlu: 0.4061\n      seed_123_mmlu: 0.3763\n      seed_456_mmlu: 0.3727\n      mmlu_mean: 0.385\n      mmlu_std_pp: 1.83\n      seed_42_ppl: 8.8157\n      seed_123_ppl: 8.8186\n      seed_456_ppl: 8.8284\n      ppl_mean: 8.821\n      ppl_std: 0.006\n      global_alloc_mmlu_std_pp: 9.57\n      global_alloc_seed_42_mmlu: 0.2527\n      global_alloc_seed_123_mmlu: 0.3807\n      global_alloc_seed_456_mmlu: 0.4382\n      narrative_issue: \"uniform fixes variance (σ=1.83pp) but global is catastrophic (σ=9.57pp) — method is fragile without uniform allocation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据显示 uniform allocation σ=1.83pp（低于 worst 阈值 4pp），但 global allocation\n      σ=9.57pp（远超阈值）。seed 42 的 global MMLU=25.27% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 38-44%），\n      说明 global top-k 在 30% 下 allocation 高度依赖 predictor 初始化——某些 seed 的 predictor\n      恰好 starve 了 knowledge-critical layers（L12-L20 region），导致 MMLU 崩溃。\n      under worst 的 narrative：虽然 uniform 修复了方差，但这等于承认方法本身不 robust——\n      需要特定 allocation 策略才能工作。如果 uniform 是必须的，那 predictor 的 learned allocation\n      就没有 added value（claim 3 的 \"budget-constrained regime learned allocation outperforms\"\n      叙事直接矛盾）。Reviewer 会问：\"if uniform allocation is always better at 30% and\n      learned allocation is better at 40%, is the predictor just learning to approximate\n      uniform allocation at low sparsity?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S2 (Robustness): 3-seed × 2-allocation MMLU/PPL matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Violin plot showing MMLU distribution across seeds for uniform (tight) vs global (wide spread)\"\n    analysis: >\n      robustness 的 story 是 \"half-good, half-bad\"——PPL stable across seeds（σ<0.01），\n      MMLU stable under uniform（σ=1.83pp），但 global allocation 下 MMLU 变成 lottery。\n      这不是 fatal 但让 reviewer 有理由要求 5-seed 或更多 seeds 的 confidence intervals，\n      which we cannot provide for all conditions within submission timeline。\n\n  - name: reviewer_meta_assessment\n    plan_id: null\n    description: >\n      综合 reviewer 评估预测。基于所有 worst-tier 实验结果的 expected ARR scores。\n    expected_results:\n      expected_ARR_overall: 2.75\n      reviewer_1_score: 3.0\n      reviewer_1_concerns: \"Contribution is a controlled study, not a new method. Interesting negative results but not enough for Main.\"\n      reviewer_2_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_2_concerns: \"Phase transition claim unsupported. No wall-clock speedup. 14B MMLU gap unexplained.\"\n      reviewer_3_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_3_concerns: \"C1 ablation is ambiguous — 60/40 split between mask quality and optimization process is not a clear finding. BCE at 30% makes KL's practical value questionable.\"\n      meta_reviewer_decision: reject\n      meta_reviewer_note: \"All three reviewers agree the contribution is incremental. The controlled study is thorough but the framing oversells the findings.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst tier 下三路攻击同时命中：\n      (1) C1 ablation ambiguous → mask pattern framing 无法 defend，但数据不支持 clean alternative story\n      (2) No phase transition → Claim 3 (regime analysis) 是论文最 novel 的 claim，但 6-point data 不支持\n      (3) No wall-clock speedup (latency_benchmark 已确认 0.94x slowdown) → practical value 仅为\n      理论 FLOPs 节省，reviewer 会说 \"theoretical savings without actual speedup is not a deployment contribution\"\n      (4) 14B gap (MMLU 64.49 vs TEAL 71.83) 仍无解释 → generalization claim 被限制为 \"works on 8B only\"\n      (5) LongBench/MT-Bench/RULER 全面暴露 long-context 和 generation quality 的 weakness\n      综合 ARR 2.75：介于 \"borderline reject\" (3.0) 和 \"clear reject\" (2.5) 之间。\n      不会 desk reject（实验工作量大），但不够 Main。可能被建议 resubmit to Findings。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst tier 下，论文的最合理归宿是 reject from Main + accept to Findings（如果 ARR\n      允许 redirect）。核心问题不是任何单一实验失败，而是 framing 与数据的 mismatch：\n      \"mask pattern discovery\" 故事需要 C1 ablation 的 clean result（PPL ≈ KL 或 PPL ≈ vanilla BCE），\n      但得到了 ambiguous middle ground。pivot 到 direction (A) \"practical deployment guide\"\n      是 damage-minimizing 策略——承认没有 clean mechanistic story，转而强调 comprehensive\n      controlled study 的 practical value（\"我们做了别人没做过的 systematic comparison，\n      这里是 when-to-use-what recipe\"）。3-5 天重写量，deadline 前可完成。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34575,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34575},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9d7294e-da79-48fd-83a0-93196cf1e3dc","uuid":"99f1182a-3cc7-42ec-bfe9-1aacde679f87"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":402932,"duration_api_ms":404416,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  'Mask pattern discovery' framing 全面失败。C1 ablation 两条腿同时断裂：50% uniform 下\n  BCE-on-KL-targets PPL ≈ 16+（mask 质量不足以解释 KL 优势），30% forced top-k 下 BCE PPL ≈ 9.6\n  （与 KL 8.82 差距 trivial，KL 在推荐操作点无独特价值）。6-point sweep 无 phase transition，\n  三 regime 叙事退化为 smooth quadratic。此时必须 pivot。推荐方向 (A) practical deployment guide：\n  paper 核心变为 3-model × 4-sparsity × 2-allocation × 2-loss controlled study，贡献是 actionable recipe，\n  title 类似 \"When Does KL Distillation Help Sparse Inference? A Controlled Study\"。\n  所有已有实验数据（含 negative results）重新组织为 recipe 维度。3-5 天重写 §1-§3，无需新实验。\n  ARR 2.5-3.0，冲 Findings 或 Industry Track 更稳。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: c1_ablation_eval_uniform\n    plan_id: c1_ablation_bce_kl_targets\n    description: >\n      C1 ablation 核心实验：用 KL-derived oracle masks 训练的 BCE predictor，在 50% uniform allocation\n      下评估。测试 mask pattern quality 是否足以解释 KL 优势。\n    expected_results:\n      wt2_ppl_uniform_50pct: 16.2\n      wt2_ppl_global_50pct: 15.4\n      reference_kl_50pct_uniform_ppl: 11.96\n      reference_vanilla_bce_50pct_ppl: 22.51\n      residual_gap_vs_kl: 4.24\n      residual_gap_vs_vanilla_bce: 6.31\n      mask_quality_explains_pct: 59.4\n      optimization_process_explains_pct: 40.6\n      oracle_agreement_at_50pct_uniform: 0.91\n      eval_sparsity: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      c1_ablation_bce_kl_targets_s42 在 native ~61% sparsity 下 PPL=9.29、oracle agreement=97.8%，\n      看似 mask transfer 成功。但该结果是 per-token sparsity 下的 best-case——predictor 自行选择\n      pruning 分布。强制 50% uniform allocation 改变了两个维度：(1) sparsity level 从 61% 降到 50%\n      理应降低 PPL，但 (2) uniform allocation 移除了 predictor 的 per-layer adaptive budget，\n      暴露 BCE 优化器在 off-distribution allocation 下的脆弱性。\n      关键机制：KL 训练时全 forward pass 的 coupled gradient 让 predictor 隐式学会了 allocation-robust\n      的 mask pattern，而 BCE 仅学到 per-neuron 的 binary classification boundary——在 native sparsity\n      下精确匹配 oracle，但换 allocation 策略后迅速退化。oracle agreement 从 97.8% 降至 ~91%，\n      看似只有 7pp 差异，但在 50% sparsity 的 critical regime 下这 7% 的 mask error 被放大。\n      PPL 16.2 高于 KL 的 11.96（gap=4.24），但显著低于 vanilla BCE 的 22.51（gap=6.31），\n      说明 mask quality 解释了约 59% 的 KL 优势，剩余 41% 归因于 optimization process。\n      这个 59/41 的分割恰恰是 worst case——既不能说 \"mask pattern is everything\"（residual gap 4.24 太大），\n      也不能说 \"mask pattern is nothing\"（确实帮了 6.31 PPL），无法支撑任何简洁叙事。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 3 (C1 Ablation): 新增行 'BCE-on-KL-targets, 50% uniform' PPL=16.2，与 KL uniform=11.96、vanilla BCE=22.51 对比\"\n      - \"Table 1 (Main Results): 无法新增，但 C1 ablation 的 ambiguous 结果削弱 Table 1 中 KL vs BCE 的 framing\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4 bar chart: 三条柱 KL(11.96) / BCE-on-KL-targets(16.2) / vanilla-BCE(22.51)，中间柱的高度让 'mask quality explains KL advantage' 叙事无法成立\"\n    analysis: >\n      mask quality 解释了 KL 优势的 ~60%，但剩余 ~40% 的 gap 过大。Reviewer 会问：'so what IS the\n      explanation?'——而我们既不能说 gradient coupling（§3.6 已降为 suggestive），也不能说 mask pattern\n      （C1 ablation 刚打脸）。framing 陷入 no-man's-land。\n\n  - name: bce_30pct_forced_topk\n    plan_id: bce_30pct_forced_topk\n    description: >\n      BCE predictor 在 30% sparsity 下通过 TEAL forced top-k 评估。填 Table 2 gap，\n      测试 KL 在推荐操作点是否有独特价值。\n    expected_results:\n      wt2_ppl_teal_global_30pct: 9.62\n      reference_kl_30pct_uniform_ppl: 8.82\n      reference_teal_vanilla_30pct_ppl: 10.97\n      ppl_gap_vs_kl: 0.80\n      ppl_gap_vs_teal_vanilla: 1.35\n      arc_challenge_acc_norm: 0.398\n      winogrande_acc: 0.661\n      mmlu_acc: 0.362\n      gsm8k_exact_match: 0.071\n      actual_sparsity: 0.30\n    result_rationale: >\n      30% sparsity 是 budget-surplus regime——保留 70% 神经元，任务本质上 \"太容易\"。\n      BCE 在 50% 下训练时（bce_isocompute_v3 系列）PPL=27-28，灾难性；但 30% forced top-k\n      完全不同：(1) TEAL allocation 在 30% 下更均匀（每层保留 ≥60%），per-neuron BCE scoring\n      与 global top-k 的冲突小得多；(2) magnitude-based scoring 在低 sparsity 下本身就够好\n      （TEAL vanilla 30%=10.97 vs 50%=23.31，差 2×），BCE 的 learned scoring 只需微小改进\n      就能接近 KL；(3) 现有 kl_bce_f1_oracle 数据显示 BCE F1=0.61 vs KL=0.54——BCE 在\n      per-neuron 精度上实际更高，只是在 global reallocation 下这种精度优势被削弱。\n      在 30% 这种\"奢侈\"sparsity 下，per-neuron 精度 ≈ global quality，所以 BCE 和 KL 收敛。\n      PPL gap 仅 0.80（KL 8.82 vs BCE 9.62），MMLU gap ~4pp（KL 40.6% vs BCE 36.2%），\n      均在 noise margin 内。Reviewer 会直接问：\"why not just use BCE at 30%?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 2 (Sparsity Sweep): 新增 BCE 30% 行，PPL=9.62，与 KL 30%=8.82 并列\"\n      - \"Table 5 (Downstream): BCE 30% downstream 与 KL 30% 差距全部 <5pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: BCE 30% 点紧贴 KL 30% 点，两者在 PPL-efficiency 曲线上几乎重叠，KL 的 Pareto 优势仅在 ≥40% 才显现\"\n    analysis: >\n      KL 在推荐操作点（30%）的独特价值蒸发。PPL 差 0.80、MMLU 差 ~4pp——一个 reviewer 可以\n      argue this is meaningful，但另一个会说 \"within noise / trivial\"。关键问题：如果 30% 是\n      practical recommendation，而 KL 和 BCE 在 30% 表现相当，那 paper 的 contribution 是什么？\n      只有 ≥50% 才能看到 KL 的大幅优势，但 50% 的 downstream collapse 使该操作点无部署价值。\n\n  - name: kl_sparsity25_s42\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      KL predictor 训练 target=25% sparsity。6-point sweep 的最低 sparsity 点。\n    expected_results:\n      status: failed\n      actual_sparsity: 0.208\n      target_sparsity: 0.25\n      lambda_final: 5000\n      lambda_max_cap: 5000\n      constraint_satisfied: false\n      sparsity_trajectory: \"40%→28%→22%→21%→20.8%, stuck\"\n      wt2_ppl: null\n      training_steps: 1000\n      wall_clock_sec: 2700\n      failure_mode: \"Lagrangian cannot push sparsity to 25% — predictor architecture has implicit floor ~20% from natural activation patterns\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      kl_sparsity30 的历史已经预示了这个失败：v1 和 v2 都卡在 28.1%（target 30%），v3 靠\n      lambda_max=5000 才勉强到 28.5%。25% target 更难——需要保留 75% 的神经元，而 predictor\n      的 initial state（从 random init 经 Gumbel-sigmoid）天然倾向 ~40% sparsity。\n      Lagrangian 需要把 sparsity 从 40% 压到 25%，意味着 lambda 必须主导 loss landscape，\n      压制 KL divergence objective。但当 lambda 过大时，predictor 退化为 \"全开\" 模式，\n      sparsity 从 40% 降到 ~21% 后触底——这是 SwiGLU gate activation 的 natural floor，\n      即使不做任何 pruning 也有 ~20% 的神经元 gate value ≈ 0。\n      结果：无法评估、Table 有空缺。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 25% 行标注 '†训练未收敛' 或留空\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sweep curve 缺少最左端数据点，5 点而非 6 点\"\n    analysis: >\n      关键空缺。没有 25% 数据点意味着：(1) 无法确认 sweep 曲线左端行为；(2) Reviewer 会质疑\n      method 在低 sparsity 下的 applicability；(3) 5 点 vs 6 点对 piecewise fit 的 statistical\n      power 进一步下降。\n\n  - name: kl_sparsity35_s42\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      KL predictor 训练 target=35% sparsity。填补 30%-40% 之间的中间点。\n    expected_results:\n      actual_sparsity: 0.337\n      target_sparsity: 0.35\n      lambda_final: 3000\n      constraint_satisfied: true\n      wt2_ppl_pertoken: 8.05\n      wt2_ppl_teal_global: 9.42\n      wt2_ppl_uniform: 8.28\n      arc_challenge_acc_norm: 0.412\n      winogrande_acc: 0.672\n      mmlu_acc: 0.351\n      gsm8k_exact_match: 0.058\n      training_steps: 1000\n    result_rationale: >\n      35% 在 30% 和 40% 之间，Lagrangian 应能收敛（30% 最终成功，40% 直接成功）。\n      PPL 预测基于已有数据的 smooth interpolation：30% global=8.98、40% global=10.12，\n      线性插值给出 ~9.5，但实际曲线在低 sparsity 端略 concave（KL 在 budget-surplus 下\n      性能降解更缓慢），所以 35% global ≈ 9.42。这恰恰是 worst case 的关键证据——\n      35% 点完美落在 30% 和 40% 的线性插值上，没有任何 inflection point 或 regime boundary。\n      如果存在 phase transition，应该在 30%-40% 之间看到斜率突变，但 35% 的 PPL 9.42\n      精确匹配线性趋势。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 35% 行 PPL=9.42\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sweep curve: 35% 点落在 30%-40% 的线性连接线上，无 inflection\"\n    analysis: >\n      最具破坏力的数据点。35% 的 smooth interpolation 直接否定了 \"budget-surplus → budget-constrained\n      regime boundary exists between 30-40%\" 的说法。原叙事中 30% uniform wins、40% global wins\n      的 \"non-monotonic allocation preference\" 现在看起来只是 noise——35% 的 allocation preference\n      如果也是 ambiguous（uniform 和 global 差距 <2pp），那 regime boundary 就不存在。\n\n  - name: kl_sparsity45_s42\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      KL predictor 训练 target=45% sparsity。填补 40%-50% 之间的中间点。\n    expected_results:\n      actual_sparsity: 0.432\n      target_sparsity: 0.45\n      lambda_final: 5000\n      constraint_satisfied: false\n      wt2_ppl_pertoken: 9.81\n      wt2_ppl_teal_global: 10.65\n      wt2_ppl_uniform: 10.32\n      arc_challenge_acc_norm: 0.368\n      winogrande_acc: 0.648\n      mmlu_acc: 0.298\n      gsm8k_exact_match: 0.032\n      training_steps: 1000\n      sparsity_note: \"actual 43.2% vs target 45%, Lagrangian undershoots by 1.8pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      45% 介于 40%（成功，actual=39.8%）和 50%（成功，actual=49.8%）之间。Lagrangian\n      略有 undershoot（1.8pp），类似 30% 的情况但不严重到 fail。PPL 10.65 global\n      在 40% 的 10.12 和 50% 的 11.79 之间 smooth interpolation。\n      关键在下游：MMLU 29.8% 已经接近 random（25%），但 40% 时还有 38.1%。如果存在\n      \"capacity cliff\" phase transition，应该在 45% 看到 MMLU 从 38% 急跌到 ~28%，\n      但实际上 45% 给出 29.8%——这是 smooth degradation 而非 cliff。40%→45% MMLU\n      差 8.3pp、45%→50% 差 2.1pp，斜率 decreasing 而非 increasing，说明是 approaching\n      asymptote（random baseline）而非 phase transition。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 45% 行 PPL=10.65, MMLU=29.8%\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sweep curve: 45% 点继续 smooth 趋势，MMLU 曲线 approaching random floor without sharp transition\"\n    analysis: >\n      MMLU 的 \"cliff\" 在数据 densification 后消失。40%→50% 看似 dramatic drop（38.1→27.8，\n      -10.3pp），但加入 45%（29.8%）后变成两段 smooth decline：40→45 降 8.3pp、45→50 降 2.0pp。\n      不是 cliff，是 gradual approach to random floor。\n\n  - name: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt_aggregate\n    plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n    description: >\n      6-point sweep 聚合分析：25%/30%/35%/40%/45%/50%。Piecewise regression 测试\n      三 regime 叙事 vs smooth quadratic。\n    expected_results:\n      available_points: 5\n      missing_points: [\"25%\"]\n      ppl_values_global:\n        sp30: 8.98\n        sp35: 9.42\n        sp40: 10.12\n        sp45: 10.65\n        sp50: 11.79\n      quadratic_fit_r2: 0.987\n      piecewise_3segment_fit_r2: 0.993\n      piecewise_improvement_over_quadratic: 0.006\n      f_test_pvalue_piecewise_vs_quadratic: 0.42\n      regime_boundary_30_40_evidence: \"none — 35% interpolates linearly\"\n      regime_boundary_40_50_evidence: \"none — 45% interpolates linearly\"\n      mmlu_values:\n        sp30_uniform: 0.406\n        sp35: 0.351\n        sp40_global: 0.381\n        sp45: 0.298\n        sp50_uniform: 0.278\n      mmlu_smooth_degradation: true\n      mmlu_phase_transition_evidence: \"none — monotonic decline approaching random floor\"\n      allocation_preference_at_35pct: \"ambiguous (uniform 8.28 vs global 9.42, confounded by sparsity mismatch)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      5 个可用数据点（25% 缺失）的 PPL sweep 完美拟合 quadratic：PPL ≈ 6.12 + 0.03s + 0.15s²\n      （s = sparsity %），R² = 0.987。Piecewise 3-segment 拟合 R² = 0.993，比 quadratic\n      仅提升 0.006，F-test p=0.42 远不显著——增加两个 breakpoint 参数不 justified。\n      原叙事的三 regime 基于 3 个点（30/40/50）的 apparent inflection，但 densified sampling\n      填入 35% 和 45% 后，所有 \"inflection\" 消失为 smooth curve。MMLU 的下降也是 monotonic：\n      40.6→35.1→38.1→29.8→27.8，40% 的 38.1% 看似 \"recovery\"，但那是 global allocation\n      的效果（之前 30% 用 uniform），allocation × sparsity confound 未被控制。\n      在所有 sparsity 用同一 allocation 评估后（e.g., 全用 global），MMLU 严格递减，无 non-monotonicity。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 4 (Sparsity Sweep): 完整 5-point sweep，右侧列标注 quadratic fit residuals\"\n      - \"Table S1 (Supplementary): Piecewise vs quadratic fit comparison statistics\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: PPL vs sparsity scatter + quadratic fit curve (R²=0.987)，无 visible phase transition\"\n      - \"Fig 5b: MMLU vs sparsity，monotonic decline approaching 25% floor，与 PPL 趋势一致\"\n      - \"Fig S1: Residual plot of piecewise vs quadratic，residuals indistinguishable\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 regime 叙事不成立。数据支持的 simplest model 是 smooth quadratic degradation。\n      \"Non-monotonic allocation preference\" 是 allocation × sparsity confound 的 artifact——\n      在控制 allocation 后消失。Reviewer 2 会写：\"The claimed phase transition is not\n      supported by the data. A simple quadratic fits equally well.\"\n\n  - name: plan_010_longbench\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      LongBench English subset (4K-32K tokens)。所有条件（KL-only, BCE+comp, SPON, SPON+KL,\n      training-free baselines）。测试 predictor 在长序列上的泛化能力。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_narrativeqa: 7.3\n      dense_qasper: 13.4\n      dense_gov_report: 30.5\n      dense_multi_news: 2.5\n      dense_avg: 13.4\n      kl_30_uniform_narrativeqa: 4.1\n      kl_30_uniform_qasper: 6.2\n      kl_30_uniform_gov_report: 17.0\n      kl_30_uniform_multi_news: 18.0\n      kl_30_uniform_avg: 11.3\n      kl_50_global_narrativeqa: 1.8\n      kl_50_global_qasper: 2.1\n      kl_50_global_gov_report: 8.4\n      kl_50_global_multi_news: 14.2\n      kl_50_global_avg: 6.6\n      teal_30_narrativeqa: 3.5\n      teal_30_qasper: 5.8\n      teal_30_gov_report: 15.2\n      teal_30_multi_news: 16.8\n      teal_30_avg: 10.3\n      teal_50_narrativeqa: 0.9\n      teal_50_qasper: 1.2\n      teal_50_gov_report: 4.1\n      teal_50_multi_news: 10.5\n      teal_50_avg: 4.2\n      kl_30_vs_dense_retention: 0.55\n      kl_50_vs_dense_retention: 0.31\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_advantage: \"+1.0 avg (+9.7%)\"\n      multi_news_anomaly: \"KL 30% multi_news=18.0 > dense=2.5，疑似 format mismatch / generation collapse into repetitive text inflating ROUGE\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      longbench_dense_v6 和 longbench_kl30_uniform_v6 的已有数据已经暗示了问题：\n      (1) dense baseline 本身就很弱（narrativeqa=7.3，相比 GPT-4 的 ~25），说明 Llama-3.1-8B\n      在 LongBench 上不是 competitive baseline；(2) KL 30% 相对 dense 下降 ~45%（avg 11.3 vs 13.4），\n      虽然比 TEAL 好一点，但绝对值太低没有实用意义。\n      更糟糕的是 multi_news 异常：KL 30% 得分 18.0 远高于 dense 的 2.5。这几乎必然是评估 bug\n      ——sparse model 生成退化为重复文本，而 ROUGE-L 对重复文本敏感（与 reference 中重复出现的\n      n-gram 匹配），导致假高分。这个 anomaly 会被 reviewer 抓住，要求重新评估。\n      整体来看：KL vs TEAL 的 advantage 在长序列上仅 ~10%（远低于 short-context 的 ~25%），\n      且所有 sparse 方法在 LongBench 上表现都很差——这是 sparse inference 的 fundamental limitation，\n      不是我们的 method 特有问题，但 reviewer 不关心这个区分。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 6 (LongBench): 4 tasks × 5 conditions，dense 作为上界，大面积红色（显著退化）\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: LongBench per-task grouped bar chart，所有 sparse 方法的 bars 都远低于 dense\"\n      - \"Fig 7 inset: KL 30% vs TEAL 30% 的 relative advantage（+10%）在长序列上收窄到在 short-context 的一半以下\"\n    analysis: >\n      LongBench 结果对论文的两个打击：(1) 绝对性能太低，reviewer 会质疑 \"这种 quality 水平\n      有什么部署价值\"；(2) KL 的相对优势在长序列上缩小，因为 predictor 是在 2048-token\n      序列上训练的，超出训练长度后 prediction quality 下降。这暴露了一个未在论文中讨论的\n      limitation：sparse predictor 的 sequence-length generalization。\n\n  - name: plan_011_mtbench\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      MT-Bench 评估 (GPT-4o judge)。80 multi-turn questions, 8 categories。\n      测试 instruction-following quality under sparsity。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_score: 6.82\n      kl_30_uniform_score: 5.41\n      kl_50_global_score: 3.68\n      teal_30_score: 5.12\n      teal_50_score: 2.95\n      bce_isocompute_50_score: 3.22\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_delta: \"+0.29\"\n      category_breakdown_kl_30:\n        writing: 6.1\n        roleplay: 5.8\n        reasoning: 4.2\n        math: 3.1\n        coding: 4.5\n        extraction: 6.3\n        stem: 5.2\n        humanities: 5.9\n      turn2_degradation_kl_30: \"-0.8 vs turn1\"\n      turn2_degradation_kl_50: \"-1.9 vs turn1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      MT-Bench 测试 multi-turn coherence，sparse inference 的 per-token noise 在多轮中累积。\n      dense Llama-3.1-8B MT-Bench 典型分 ~6.8。KL 30% 在 short-context PPL 上只差 0.82\n      （8.82 vs 6.12，ratio 1.44），但 MT-Bench 是生成任务——PPL 的 1.44 ratio 在 autoregressive\n      decoding 中累积，每个 token 的 slightly-wrong prediction 会 compound。\n      30% sparsity 下 turn-1 约 5.8，turn-2 降到 ~5.0（turn-2 依赖 turn-1 的 generated context，\n      sparse prediction 引入的 drift 在 turn-2 放大）。平均 5.41。\n      关键：KL 30% vs TEAL 30% 只差 0.29（5.41 vs 5.12）——在 MT-Bench 的 1-10 scale 上\n      这是 noise-level 差异，GPT-4o judge 的 inter-rater reliability 约 ±0.5。\n      Reviewer 可以 legitimately claim \"KL and TEAL are indistinguishable on generation quality\n      at 30% sparsity\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 7 (MT-Bench): 5 conditions × overall + 8 categories\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: MT-Bench radar chart，dense(外圈) vs KL-30%(中圈) vs TEAL-30%(内圈)，math/reasoning 象限 collapse 明显\"\n      - \"Fig 8b: Turn-1 vs Turn-2 degradation，sparse 方法的 turn-2 drop 显著大于 dense\"\n    analysis: >\n      MT-Bench 进一步弱化 KL 的 practical value proposition：在 generation quality（用户真正\n      感知的维度）上，KL 30% 和 TEAL 30% 的差距远小于 PPL 暗示的差距。这支持了 \"PPL is a\n      poor proxy for downstream generation quality\" 的说法——但该说法反过来也削弱了论文自身\n      以 PPL 为核心指标的可信度。math/reasoning 的 severe degradation 是 expected（这些任务\n      对 per-token accuracy 最敏感），但 reviewer 会关注这些 high-visibility categories。\n\n  - name: plan_012_ruler\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      RULER synthetic long-context (4K, 16K) × 3 task types。\n      Fine-grained capability diagnostics complementing LongBench。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_4k_niah: 0.95\n      dense_4k_vt: 0.82\n      dense_4k_cwe: 0.78\n      dense_16k_niah: 0.88\n      dense_16k_vt: 0.61\n      dense_16k_cwe: 0.52\n      kl_30_4k_niah: 0.89\n      kl_30_4k_vt: 0.71\n      kl_30_4k_cwe: 0.65\n      kl_30_16k_niah: 0.62\n      kl_30_16k_vt: 0.38\n      kl_30_16k_cwe: 0.29\n      kl_50_4k_niah: 0.72\n      kl_50_4k_vt: 0.48\n      kl_50_4k_cwe: 0.41\n      kl_50_16k_niah: 0.35\n      kl_50_16k_vt: 0.21\n      kl_50_16k_cwe: 0.15\n      teal_30_4k_niah: 0.86\n      teal_30_4k_vt: 0.67\n      teal_30_4k_cwe: 0.59\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_avg_4k: \"+4.3pp\"\n      kl_30_vs_teal_30_avg_16k: \"+2.1pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RULER 的 NIAH (needle-in-a-haystack) 是 attention-dependent task，sparsity 主要影响\n      FFN 而非 attention，所以 4K 下退化相对温和（KL 30%: 0.89 vs dense 0.95）。\n      但 VT (variable tracking) 和 CWE (common-words extraction) 需要 cross-position reasoning，\n      FFN 的 capacity loss 通过 attention→FFN→attention 链式传播。16K 下所有 tasks 严重退化：\n      KL 30% NIAH 0.62（vs dense 0.88，-26pp），说明 predictor 在长序列中段的 attention output\n      分布 shift 超出训练时见过的范围。\n      KL vs TEAL 的 advantage 在 4K 下 ~4pp，16K 下缩小到 ~2pp——与 LongBench 一致：\n      predictor 的泛化优势随序列长度衰减。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table 8 (RULER): 3 tasks × 2 lengths × 4 conditions\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: RULER heatmap (task × length × condition)，颜色从绿(dense)到红(sparse 50%)，16K 列大面积红色\"\n    analysis: >\n      RULER 诊断出精确的失败模式：不是 \"sparse model cannot do long-context\"（4K 下还行），\n      而是 \"predictor trained on 2K cannot generalize to 16K\"。这是一个 fixable limitation\n      （train on longer sequences），但在当前论文中是 open gap。reviewer 12 会建议 future work。\n      更根本的问题：RULER 让 \"sparse inference as deployment-ready\" 的 narrative 难以为继——\n      实际部署需要 long-context capability，而我们的 method 在 16K 下退化 ~30-40%。\n\n  - name: kl_30pct_3seed_robustness\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      KL 30% uniform 3-seed robustness 分析（已有数据汇总 + 新 seed 预测）。\n      测试 headline numbers 的可复现性。\n    expected_results:\n      seed_42_mmlu: 0.4061\n      seed_123_mmlu: 0.3763\n      seed_456_mmlu: 0.3727\n      mmlu_mean: 0.385\n      mmlu_std_pp: 1.83\n      seed_42_ppl: 8.8157\n      seed_123_ppl: 8.8186\n      seed_456_ppl: 8.8284\n      ppl_mean: 8.821\n      ppl_std: 0.006\n      global_alloc_mmlu_std_pp: 9.57\n      global_alloc_seed_42_mmlu: 0.2527\n      global_alloc_seed_123_mmlu: 0.3807\n      global_alloc_seed_456_mmlu: 0.4382\n      narrative_issue: \"uniform fixes variance (σ=1.83pp) but global is catastrophic (σ=9.57pp) — method is fragile without uniform allocation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据显示 uniform allocation σ=1.83pp（低于 worst 阈值 4pp），但 global allocation\n      σ=9.57pp（远超阈值）。seed 42 的 global MMLU=25.27% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 38-44%），\n      说明 global top-k 在 30% 下 allocation 高度依赖 predictor 初始化——某些 seed 的 predictor\n      恰好 starve 了 knowledge-critical layers（L12-L20 region），导致 MMLU 崩溃。\n      under worst 的 narrative：虽然 uniform 修复了方差，但这等于承认方法本身不 robust——\n      需要特定 allocation 策略才能工作。如果 uniform 是必须的，那 predictor 的 learned allocation\n      就没有 added value（claim 3 的 \"budget-constrained regime learned allocation outperforms\"\n      叙事直接矛盾）。Reviewer 会问：\"if uniform allocation is always better at 30% and\n      learned allocation is better at 40%, is the predictor just learning to approximate\n      uniform allocation at low sparsity?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table S2 (Robustness): 3-seed × 2-allocation MMLU/PPL matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Violin plot showing MMLU distribution across seeds for uniform (tight) vs global (wide spread)\"\n    analysis: >\n      robustness 的 story 是 \"half-good, half-bad\"——PPL stable across seeds（σ<0.01），\n      MMLU stable under uniform（σ=1.83pp），但 global allocation 下 MMLU 变成 lottery。\n      这不是 fatal 但让 reviewer 有理由要求 5-seed 或更多 seeds 的 confidence intervals，\n      which we cannot provide for all conditions within submission timeline。\n\n  - name: reviewer_meta_assessment\n    plan_id: null\n    description: >\n      综合 reviewer 评估预测。基于所有 worst-tier 实验结果的 expected ARR scores。\n    expected_results:\n      expected_ARR_overall: 2.75\n      reviewer_1_score: 3.0\n      reviewer_1_concerns: \"Contribution is a controlled study, not a new method. Interesting negative results but not enough for Main.\"\n      reviewer_2_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_2_concerns: \"Phase transition claim unsupported. No wall-clock speedup. 14B MMLU gap unexplained.\"\n      reviewer_3_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_3_concerns: \"C1 ablation is ambiguous — 60/40 split between mask quality and optimization process is not a clear finding. BCE at 30% makes KL's practical value questionable.\"\n      meta_reviewer_decision: reject\n      meta_reviewer_note: \"All three reviewers agree the contribution is incremental. The controlled study is thorough but the framing oversells the findings.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst tier 下三路攻击同时命中：\n      (1) C1 ablation ambiguous → mask pattern framing 无法 defend，但数据不支持 clean alternative story\n      (2) No phase transition → Claim 3 (regime analysis) 是论文最 novel 的 claim，但 6-point data 不支持\n      (3) No wall-clock speedup (latency_benchmark 已确认 0.94x slowdown) → practical value 仅为\n      理论 FLOPs 节省，reviewer 会说 \"theoretical savings without actual speedup is not a deployment contribution\"\n      (4) 14B gap (MMLU 64.49 vs TEAL 71.83) 仍无解释 → generalization claim 被限制为 \"works on 8B only\"\n      (5) LongBench/MT-Bench/RULER 全面暴露 long-context 和 generation quality 的 weakness\n      综合 ARR 2.75：介于 \"borderline reject\" (3.0) 和 \"clear reject\" (2.5) 之间。\n      不会 desk reject（实验工作量大），但不够 Main。可能被建议 resubmit to Findings。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst tier 下，论文的最合理归宿是 reject from Main + accept to Findings（如果 ARR\n      允许 redirect）。核心问题不是任何单一实验失败，而是 framing 与数据的 mismatch：\n      \"mask pattern discovery\" 故事需要 C1 ablation 的 clean result（PPL ≈ KL 或 PPL ≈ vanilla BCE），\n      但得到了 ambiguous middle ground。pivot 到 direction (A) \"practical deployment guide\"\n      是 damage-minimizing 策略——承认没有 clean mechanistic story，转而强调 comprehensive\n      controlled study 的 practical value（\"我们做了别人没做过的 systematic comparison，\n      这里是 when-to-use-what recipe\"）。3-5 天重写量，deadline 前可完成。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a9d7294e-da79-48fd-83a0-93196cf1e3dc","total_cost_usd":0.74878925,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34575,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":19886,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":